      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(qqbot): add timeout to remote media URL fetches",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\nQQBot remote media downloads accepted HTTPS media URLs and delegated them through the platform media adapter without a request deadline. If a remote media host stalled before completing the fetch, inbound attachment handling or outbound remote-media send preparation could wait indefinitely.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\nThe shared media runtime already supports guarded media request timeouts. This PR wires QQBot's media adapter contract through to that runtime and gives `downloadFile` a 120s remote media fetch deadline while preserving the existing HTTPS and SSRF policy checks.\n\n## User Impact\nStalled QQBot media URLs now fail and return `null` through the existing error path instead of wedging the media pipeline forever.\n\n## Evidence\n- Focused test: `pnpm vitest run extensions/qqbot/src/engine/utils/file-utils.test.ts` -> 6 passed.\n- Format/lint: `pnpm exec oxfmt --check --threads=1 extensions/qqbot/src/engine/adapter/types.ts extensions/qqbot/src/bridge/bootstrap.ts extensions/qqbot/src/engine/utils/file-utils.ts extensions/qqbot/src/engine/utils/file-utils.test.ts && pnpm exec oxlint extensions/qqbot/src/engine/adapter/types.ts extensions/qqbot/src/bridge/bootstrap.ts extensions/qqbot/src/engine/utils/file-utils.ts extensions/qqbot/src/engine/utils/file-utils.test.ts` -> passed.\n- Whitespace: `git diff --check` -> clean.\n- Collision check before opening: open PR changed-files query for `extensions/qqbot/src/bridge/bootstrap.ts`, `extensions/qqbot/src/engine/utils/file-utils.ts`, and `extensions/qqbot/src/engine/adapter/types.ts` returned no open PRs.\n\n## Proof\nRegression contract: `downloadFile` now asserts the QQBot platform adapter receives `timeoutMs: QQBOT_REMOTE_MEDIA_FETCH_TIMEOUT_MS` together with the existing QQBot SSRF policy. That verifies the production QQBot boundary now reaches the shared media runtime timeout path.\n\nControlled QQBot `downloadFile` stall transcript. The harness keeps the URL at the `downloadFile` boundary production-shaped (`https://media.qq.com/...`), registers a test platform adapter, confirms the adapter receives the production 120s timeout, then uses a local stalled transport capped at 500ms so the proof run does not wait two minutes:\n\n```text\n$ pnpm exec tsx --input-type=module - <<'SCRIPT'\n# registers a platform adapter, calls downloadFile(\"https://media.qq.com/redacted/photo.png\"),\n# lets a local media server accept the request while withholding headers,\n# and reports the existing downloadFile catch/null path\nSCRIPT\nadapter: received timeoutMs=120000\nstall-server: accepted media request; intentionally withholding headers\n[qqbot:downloadFile] FAILED url=https://media.qq.com/redacted/photo.png error=adapter fetch aborted; production timeoutMs=120000\ndownloadFile: result=null elapsed=508ms\n[qqbot:downloadFile] cause=harness timeout after 500ms\ndownloadFile: filesWritten=0\n```\n\nWhy this covers the bug: before this PR, `downloadFile` did not provide a deadline to the adapter/runtime media fetch. After this PR, the adapter receives the production timeout and a stalled fetch returns through the existing `downloadFile` error path as `null` without writing a file.\n\nWhat was not tested: live QQBot traffic. This is controlled adapter/runtime proof, not a live QQBot media URL capture; secrets, tokens, and media IDs are not involved.\n",
        "branch": "alix/qqbot-remote-media-fetch-timeout",
